1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,306
Voice clones are everywhere. The people
they belong to don't know,

2
00:00:04,346 --> 00:00:06,675
and don't get paid. This is Residuals.

3
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:13,428
Residuals uses AI to find a registered
voice in any audio, even as a clone,

4
00:00:13,468 --> 00:00:16,500
and pays its owner a royalty through
PayPal.

5
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:21,943
Consent comes first. Only the owner can
enrol their voice,

6
00:00:21,983 --> 00:00:25,817
by recording a consent statement and
reading a random phrase,

7
00:00:25,857 --> 00:00:30,198
so an old recording can't pass. Then they
set terms in plain English,

8
00:00:30,238 --> 00:00:33,350
and Gemini turns them into a policy they
confirm.

9
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,447
Detection runs on a Kaggle GPU: speech
detection, ECAPA voice embeddings,

10
00:00:42,487 --> 00:00:45,868
a clone detector, Whisper, and Gemini for
the use type.

11
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,747
A brand pre-clears its radio ad. The
timeline shows Mara Vell's voice,

12
00:00:50,787 --> 00:00:55,465
as an AI clone, and Ivy Calder's.
Brightline holds licences for both,

13
00:00:55,505 --> 00:00:59,950
so each is priced by its owner's own
terms: $30 a minute for ads.

14
00:01:07,090 --> 00:01:11,224
One PayPal invoice covers the licensed
minutes. When it's paid,

15
00:01:11,264 --> 00:01:14,139
PayPal sends a signed webhook. We verify
it,

16
00:01:14,179 --> 00:01:17,518
and a PayPal Payout sends each owner their
royalty,

17
00:01:17,558 --> 00:01:20,540
minus a 10% platform fee shown on every
line.

18
00:01:25,270 --> 00:01:28,391
Payouts are idempotent per invoice and
voice,

19
00:01:28,431 --> 00:01:31,170
so a webhook retry can never pay twice.

20
00:01:33,270 --> 00:01:38,204
No licence? QuickClips gets a retroactive
licence offer instead of a lawsuit.

21
00:01:38,244 --> 00:01:43,307
But Mara never allows political use, so
the Measure 12 ad gets no offer at all.

22
00:01:43,347 --> 00:01:45,995
It's blocked, and the owners are alerted.

23
00:01:57,090 --> 00:02:02,360
Each owner sees every use, what it earned,
and a hash-chained ledger in AG Grid,

24
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:04,590
with the PayPal IDs on every row.

25
00:02:12,790 --> 00:02:17,983
On synthetic test voices, clones still
match their owner. Clone detection is weaker,

26
00:02:18,023 --> 00:02:20,515
so it's shown as evidence, never billed.

27
00:02:22,790 --> 00:02:27,322
Every voice here is a fictional synthetic
persona. Residuals: your voice,

28
00:02:27,362 --> 00:02:29,053
your terms, your royalties.
